course: dictionary
lesson: 4841
title: Hydraulic: power from liquid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know a hard word to understand a text. Look at the words around it, which are its context, because they leave clues. «A cherry picker lifts workers on a platform at the end of a folding hydraulic arm.» The arm lifts the platform, so hydraulic must describe how the arm works.
explain: Test your guess by swapping it into the sentence. Hydraulic means worked by the pressure of a liquid, usually oil or water, pushed through pipes. Try it: «a folding arm worked by liquid pushed through pipes» still makes sense, so the guess fits.
explain: Hydraulic is an adjective, so it describes a thing. Hydraulics is a noun: it can mean the science of liquid pressure, or the hydraulic parts of a machine. «Turning the steering wheel moves a rod and gears, and power steering helps with a motor or hydraulics (oil pushed through pipes).»
fact: Hydraulic means worked by the pressure of a liquid, usually oil or water, pushed through pipes.
fact: In a hydraulic system, a small push on liquid in a narrow pipe can make a big force in a wide pipe.
fact: Hydraulic systems work car brakes, diggers, car lifts and dentists' chairs.
fact: Hydraulic can also mean to do with moving water, as in hydraulic engineering for dams, canals and pipes.
fact: Hydraulics is a noun: the science of liquid pressure, or the hydraulic parts of a machine.
exercise: «A cherry picker lifts workers on a platform at the end of a folding hydraulic arm.» What does hydraulic describe? | *Worked by liquid pushed through pipes | Made of wood and rope | Painted bright yellow | Lighter than air
exercise: In a hydraulic system, what happens when a small push is made on liquid in a narrow pipe? | *It can make a big force in a wide pipe | It stops the liquid completely | It turns the liquid into gas | It makes only a small force
exercise: Which of these is a hydraulic machine from the lessons? | A wooden spoon | A paper clip | A bicycle chain | *A car lift
test: «Turning the steering wheel moves a rod and gears, and power steering helps with a motor or hydraulics (oil pushed through pipes).» What does hydraulics mean in this sentence? | A kind of paint | Loud music | *Oil pushed through pipes | A road map
test: Which example is hydraulic engineering? | *A dam and canal system for moving water | A wooden chair with four legs | A bag of sugar | A hand-drawn picture of a tree
exam: Jayden is not sure what hydraulic means, so he checks his guess. Which check is best? | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the picture and ignore the words | Ask someone to tell you the answer without thinking | Guess the longest answer
